(function(E){ const x = E["exam-04"] = E["exam-04"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x04-r1"] = {"id":"x04-r1","patterns":["RA-nature","GT1-ads","PARA-cause"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about an environmental report, then complete a flow-chart of a process with up to two words and three notes with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir çevre raporu hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN kararı vermeyi, sonra bir süreci gösteren akış şemasını en fazla iki kelimeyle ve üç notu metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی یک گزارش زیست‌محیطی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بعد فلوچارتِ یک فرایند را با حداکثر دو کلمه و سه یادداشت را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to check statements about a course advert as TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, watching for conditions, and to match facts to six short listings when a letter can be used more than once.","tr":"Bu derste bir kurs ilanıyla ilgili ifadeleri koşullara dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olarak kontrol etmeyi ve bir harfin birden fazla kullanılabildiği durumda bilgileri altı kısa tanıtımla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی آگهی یک دوره را با دقت به شرط‌ها به‌صورت TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN بررسی کنی و اطلاعات را به شش معرفی کوتاه وصل کنی، وقتی یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: an environmental report","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir çevre raporu","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک گزارش زیست‌محیطی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about an environmental report, then complete a flow-chart of a process with up to two words and three notes with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir çevre raporu hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN kararı vermeyi, sonra bir süreci gösteren akış şemasını en fazla iki kelimeyle ve üç notu metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی یک گزارش زیست‌محیطی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بعد فلوچارتِ یک فرایند را با حداکثر دو کلمه و سه یادداشت را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Tasks","tr":"Görev","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"3"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: the seaweed that came ashore","tr":"Bu sınav: kıyıya vuran deniz yosunu","fa":"این آزمون: جلبکی که به ساحل آمد"},"intro":{"en":"Academic Passage 1 is often about the natural world. Environmental reports follow a pattern: what the thing is, what changed, possible causes, effects, and solutions. A process (how something is made or treated) is often turned into a flow-chart.","tr":"Academic Passage 1 çoğu zaman doğayla ilgilidir. Çevre raporları bir kalıbı izler: şeyin ne olduğu, ne değiştiği, olası nedenler, etkiler ve çözümler. Bir süreç (bir şeyin nasıl yapıldığı ya da işlendiği) çoğu zaman bir akış şemasına dönüştürülür.","fa":"Academic Passage 1 اغلب درباره‌ی طبیعت است. گزارش‌های زیست‌محیطی الگویی دارند: آن چیز چیست، چه تغییری کرد، علت‌های احتمالی، اثرها و راه‌حل‌ها. یک فرایند (اینکه چیزی چطور ساخته یا عمل‌آوری می‌شود) اغلب به فلوچارت تبدیل می‌شود."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x04-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A seaweed that became a problem","tr":"Soruna dönüşen bir deniz yosunu","fa":"جلبکی که دردسر شد"},"asks":{"en":"A report on a floating seaweed: where it lives, how it suddenly spread, the possible causes, the damage it does on beaches, and how people now try to use it.","tr":"Yüzen bir deniz yosunu hakkında bir rapor: nerede yaşadığı, nasıl birden yayıldığı, olası nedenler, kumsallarda verdiği zarar ve insanların onu şimdi nasıl kullanmaya çalıştığı.","fa":"گزارشی درباره‌ی یک جلبک شناور: کجا زندگی می‌کند، چطور ناگهان گسترش یافت، علت‌های احتمالی، آسیبی که در ساحل می‌زند و اینکه مردم حالا چطور می‌خواهند از آن استفاده کنند."},"fields":["What it is","A habitat","The spread","Possible causes","Damage on the coast","Keeping it away","Uses"],"words":[{"a":"floats freely","b":"is not attached to anything","tr":"serbestçe yüzer","fa":"آزادانه شناور است"},{"a":"habitat","b":"the place where an animal lives","tr":"yaşam alanı","fa":"زیستگاه"},{"a":"shelter","b":"hide / find protection","tr":"sığınmak","fa":"پناه گرفتن"},{"a":"nutrients","b":"substances that help things grow","tr":"besin maddeleri","fa":"مواد مغذی"},{"a":"debated","b":"not agreed / still discussed","tr":"tartışmalı","fa":"محل بحث"},{"a":"rots","b":"goes bad / decays","tr":"çürür","fa":"می‌پوسد"},{"a":"gives off","b":"produces (a gas or a smell)","tr":"yayar","fa":"بیرون می‌دهد"},{"a":"clogged","b":"blocked","tr":"tıkanmış","fa":"گرفته، مسدود"},{"a":"a blow to","b":"damage to","tr":"... için bir darbe","fa":"ضربه‌ای به"},{"a":"absorb","b":"take in","tr":"emmek","fa":"جذب کردن"},{"a":"an early warning","b":"news before something arrives","tr":"erken uyarı","fa":"هشدار زودهنگام"},{"a":"a resource","b":"something useful","tr":"kaynak","fa":"منبع"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Several causes... but there is no agreement\": a statement saying scientists agree on one main cause is FALSE.","tr":"\"Birkaç neden... ama bir uzlaşma yok\": bilim insanlarının tek bir ana nedende anlaştığını söyleyen ifade FALSE’tur.","fa":"«چند علت... اما توافقی نیست»: جمله‌ای که می‌گوید دانشمندان روی یک علت اصلی توافق دارند FALSE است."},{"en":"A flow-chart follows the order of the process in the passage. Find the first step, then read on: the answers come one after another.","tr":"Akış şeması metindeki sürecin sırasını izler. İlk adımı bul, sonra okumaya devam et: cevaplar art arda gelir.","fa":"فلوچارت ترتیب فرایند در متن را دنبال می‌کند. قدم اول را پیدا کن و ادامه بده: جواب‌ها پشت سر هم می‌آیند."}],"example":{"text":"\"The jellyfish usually stay far out at sea. Only in very warm summers do large numbers reach the coast.\"","item":"Statement: Jellyfish reach the coast in large numbers every summer. TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Only in very warm summers\": not every summer.","tr":"\"Yalnızca çok sıcak yazlarda\": her yaz değil.","fa":"«فقط در تابستان‌های خیلی گرم»: نه هر تابستان."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-report","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Reports on ecosystems and the environment","tr":"Ekosistemler ve çevre üzerine raporlar","fa":"گزارش درباره‌ی زیست‌بوم‌ها و محیط زیست"},"asks":{"en":"A report in lettered paragraphs about an ecosystem or an environmental problem: what it is, why it matters, what threatens it and what is being done. Headings name each paragraph’s main idea; matching information asks where one detail is.","tr":"Bir ekosistem ya da çevre sorunu hakkında harfli paragraflardan oluşan bir rapor: ne olduğu, neden önemli olduğu, onu neyin tehdit ettiği ve neler yapıldığı. Başlıklar her paragrafın ana fikrini adlandırır; bilgi eşleştirme tek bir ayrıntının nerede olduğunu sorar.","fa":"گزارشی با پاراگراف‌های حرف‌دار درباره‌ی یک زیست‌بوم یا یک مشکل محیط‌زیستی: چیست، چرا مهم است، چه چیزی تهدیدش می‌کند و چه کاری انجام می‌شود. عنوان‌ها ایده‌ی اصلی هر پاراگراف‌اند؛ جورکردن اطلاعات می‌پرسد یک نکته‌ی جزئی کجاست."},"fields":["The economic value of the forest","An unexpected benefit","Causes of decline","Early attempts at protection","A way of measuring change","Which paragraph mentions a comparison with another region?"],"words":[{"a":"a threat to","b":"puts at risk / endangers","tr":"... için tehdit","fa":"تهدیدی برای"},{"a":"causes","b":"the reasons / what led to","tr":"nedenler","fa":"علت‌ها"},{"a":"an unexpected benefit","b":"a surprising advantage","tr":"beklenmedik bir fayda","fa":"فایده‌ای غیرمنتظره"},{"a":"economic value","b":"worth money / income from","tr":"ekonomik değer","fa":"ارزش اقتصادی"},{"a":"early attempts","b":"the first efforts / initially tried","tr":"ilk girişimler","fa":"تلاش‌های اولیه"},{"a":"a new approach","b":"a different method / instead, now","tr":"yeni bir yaklaşım","fa":"رویکردی تازه"},{"a":"measuring","b":"monitoring / recording","tr":"ölçme","fa":"اندازه‌گیری"},{"a":"restore","b":"bring back / replant","tr":"eski haline getirmek","fa":"احیا کردن"},{"a":"long-term","b":"over decades / in the future","tr":"uzun vadeli","fa":"بلندمدت"},{"a":"local communities","b":"people living nearby","tr":"yerel halk","fa":"جوامع محلی"},{"a":"a comparison","b":"unlike / whereas in","tr":"bir karşılaştırma","fa":"یک مقایسه"},{"a":"consequences","b":"effects / results","tr":"sonuçlar","fa":"پیامدها"}],"traps":[{"en":"The detail trap: one heading matches a single detail of the paragraph, not its main idea.","tr":"Ayrıntı tuzağı: bir başlık paragrafın ana fikrine değil, tek bir ayrıntısına uyar.","fa":"دام جزئیات: یک عنوان با یک نکته‌ی جزئیِ پاراگراف جور است، نه با ایده‌ی اصلی‌اش."},{"en":"Matching information: the detail may sit in a paragraph whose main idea is something else.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirme: ayrıntı, ana fikri başka bir şey olan bir paragrafta olabilir.","fa":"جورکردن اطلاعات: جزئیات ممکن است در پاراگرافی باشد که ایده‌ی اصلی‌اش چیز دیگری است."}],"example":{"text":"D  Restoring peat bogs was once thought to be simple: block the drains and wait for the water to return. Yet in many early projects the peat stayed dry for years, because the bogs had sunk below the level of the land around them.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph D:  i  Why early restoration often failed   ii  The value of peat for farming   iii  How drains are built","answer":"i","why":{"en":"\"Once thought to be simple... yet... stayed dry\" = early attempts that failed. Drains are only a detail.","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar basit sanılıyordu... ama... kuru kaldı\" = başarısız ilk girişimler. Kanallar yalnızca bir ayrıntı.","fa":"«زمانی ساده تصور می‌شد... ولی... خشک ماند» = تلاش‌های اولیه‌ی ناموفق. زهکش‌ها فقط یک نکته‌ی جزئی‌اند."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Statements, a flow-chart, notes","tr":"İfadeler, bir akış şeması, notlar","fa":"جمله‌ها، یک فلوچارت، یادداشت‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Questions 8-10: a flow-chart, NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Questions 11-13: notes, ONE WORD ONLY. Each task follows the order of the passage.","tr":"Soru 1-7: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 8-10: bir akış şeması, metinden NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Soru 11-13: notlar, ONE WORD ONLY. Her görev metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۰: یک فلوچارت، NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS از متن. سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۳: یادداشت، ONE WORD ONLY. هر تمرین به ترتیب متن جلو می‌رود."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Use the limit as a clue","tr":"Sınırı bir ipucu olarak kullan","fa":"از سقف کلمه به‌عنوان سرنخ استفاده کن"},"steps":[{"en":"For the flow-chart, find the paragraph that describes the process step by step.","tr":"Akış şeması için süreci adım adım anlatan paragrafı bul.","fa":"برای فلوچارت، پاراگرافی را پیدا کن که فرایند را قدم به قدم توضیح می‌دهد."},{"en":"Read the step around each gap and look for the same action in the passage: collect, wash, test, dry.","tr":"Her boşluğun etrafındaki adımı oku ve metinde aynı eylemi ara: collect, wash, test, dry.","fa":"قدمِ دور هر جای خالی را بخوان و همان کار را در متن پیدا کن: collect، wash، test، dry."},{"en":"Copy one or two words exactly; leave out \"the\" if the limit is tight and it is not needed.","tr":"Bir ya da iki kelimeyi aynen kopyala; sınır darsa ve gerekmiyorsa \"the\"yi çıkar.","fa":"یک یا دو کلمه را دقیق کپی کن؛ اگر سقف تنگ است و لازم نیست، «the» را حذف کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One flow-chart gap, step by step","tr":"Bir akış şeması boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالی فلوچارت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the flow-chart. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage.","text":"\"The olives are picked by hand, washed in cold water and then crushed between large stones to produce a thick paste.\"","item":"picked → washed → crushed to make a thick ___","answer":"paste","walk":[{"en":"Find the process: picked, washed, crushed.","tr":"Süreci bul: toplanır, yıkanır, ezilir.","fa":"فرایند را پیدا کن: چیده می‌شود، شسته می‌شود، له می‌شود."},{"en":"The gap follows \"a thick\": it needs a noun.","tr":"Boşluk \"a thick\"ten sonra geliyor: bir isim gerekiyor.","fa":"جای خالی بعد از «a thick» است: یک اسم لازم است."},{"en":"Copy one word: paste. \"thick\" is printed.","tr":"Tek kelime kopyala: paste. \"thick\" yazılı.","fa":"یک کلمه کپی کن: paste. «thick» چاپ شده."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Several explanations have been suggested, but none has been proved.\" Statement: \"Scientists know what caused the change.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"None has been proved\" contradicts \"scientists know\".","tr":"\"Hiçbiri kanıtlanmadı\", \"bilim insanları biliyor\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«هیچ‌کدام ثابت نشده» با «دانشمندان می‌دانند» تناقض دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"Check how certain the passage is, follow the process step by step, and stay inside the word limit.","tr":"Metnin ne kadar kesin olduğunu kontrol et, süreci adım adım takip et ve kelime sınırının içinde kal.","fa":"ببین متن چقدر قطعی است، فرایند را قدم به قدم دنبال کن و داخل سقف کلمه بمان."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x04-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"The seaweed that came ashore","tr":"Kıyıya vuran deniz yosunu","fa":"جلبکی که به ساحل آمد"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"The seaweed that came ashore\n\nSargassum is a brown seaweed unlike almost any other. Most seaweeds grow attached to rocks, but sargassum floats freely in the open ocean, kept on the surface by tiny gas-filled bladders that look like berries. For centuries it was associated above all with the Sargasso Sea, a calm area of the North Atlantic where great floating rafts of it were described by sailors, who feared that their ships might become trapped. In fact the seaweed is far too thin to stop a ship, but the stories lasted for hundreds of years.\n\nIn the open ocean, these rafts are an important habitat. Small fish, crabs and shrimps shelter among the fronds, young sea turtles hide there in their first years of life, and larger fish come to feed on the creatures that live beneath them. Some of these animals are found nowhere else, and their colours and shapes have evolved to match the seaweed so closely that they are almost impossible to see. For most of history, very little of the seaweed reached the coasts of the Caribbean, and when it did, the amounts were small enough to be ignored.\n\nThat changed in 2011. In that year, enormous quantities of sargassum began to appear in a part of the tropical Atlantic where it had rarely been seen before, stretching from the coast of West Africa towards the Gulf of Mexico. Since then, the floating belt of seaweed has returned almost every year, and in some years satellites have recorded more than ten million tonnes. Much of it is eventually pushed by winds and currents onto the beaches of the Caribbean islands, Mexico and parts of West Africa.\n\nWhy this has happened is still debated. One explanation points to rivers such as the Amazon, which carry fertilisers from farmland into the sea, providing extra nutrients for the seaweed to grow. Another suggests that dust blown from the Sahara adds nutrients when it falls on the ocean. A third links the change to unusual winds in 2009 and 2010, which may have carried seaweed out of the Sargasso Sea into warmer waters. Most researchers think several causes are probably working together, but there is no agreement about which matters most.\n\nWhen the seaweed reaches the shore, the problems begin. Piles of it a metre or more deep can cover a beach in a single night. As it rots, it gives off hydrogen sulphide, a gas that smells of rotten eggs and can cause headaches and breathing difficulties for people who live nearby. In shallow water, thick mats block out the light, killing seagrass and the animals that depend on it. On some beaches, young turtles that hatch in the sand struggle to reach the sea through the seaweed. Fishing boats find their nets and engines clogged, and holidaymakers stay away from beaches that smell bad, a serious blow to economies that depend on tourism.\n\nGovernments and hotels have tried several ways of keeping the seaweed off the beaches. Floating barriers placed out at sea can guide it away from the shore, and specially designed boats collect it before it lands. On the beach itself, the usual answer is still people with rakes and lorries, a slow and costly job that must be repeated day after day during the worst months. Heavy machines can clear a beach quickly, but they also remove large amounts of sand and can crush turtle nests, so many places now limit their use.\n\nIncreasingly, however, the question is not only how to get rid of sargassum but how to use it. The most obvious use is as a fertiliser. Before it can be spread on fields, the seaweed must be collected before it starts to rot, then washed with fresh water to remove the sea salt, which would damage crops. It must also be tested for heavy metals, because sargassum can absorb substances such as arsenic from the water. Only when it has passed these tests is it dried and mixed into compost.\n\nOther uses are being explored too. In Mexico, one company has pressed the dried seaweed into building blocks that have been used to construct houses, and others have turned it into paper. Meanwhile, scientists are working on systems that use satellite images to give early warnings of large mats heading for the coast, so that communities have time to prepare. None of these solutions removes the problem, and all of them are still small compared with the size of the blooms, but together they may turn an unwelcome visitor into a resource.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Like most seaweeds, sargassum grows attached to rocks.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"sargassum floats freely in the open ocean","why":{"en":"\"Most seaweeds grow attached to rocks, but sargassum floats freely in the open ocean.\"","tr":"\"Çoğu deniz yosunu kayalara tutunarak büyür ama sargassum açık denizde serbestçe yüzer.\"","fa":"«بیشتر جلبک‌ها چسبیده به صخره رشد می‌کنند، اما سارگاسوم آزادانه در دریای باز شناور است»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Ships were often trapped by seaweed in the Sargasso Sea.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"In fact the seaweed is far too thin to stop a ship","why":{"en":"Sailors feared it, but \"in fact the seaweed is far too thin to stop a ship\".","tr":"Denizciler bundan korkuyordu ama \"aslında yosun bir gemiyi durduramayacak kadar ince\".","fa":"دریانوردها از آن می‌ترسیدند، اما «در واقع جلبک برای نگه داشتن یک کشتی خیلی نازک است»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Some of the animals that live among sargassum are not found in any other habitat.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Some of these animals are found nowhere else","why":{"en":"\"Found nowhere else\" = not found in any other habitat.","tr":"\"Başka hiçbir yerde bulunmuyor\" = başka bir yaşam alanında yok.","fa":"«هیچ جای دیگری پیدا نمی‌شوند» یعنی در زیستگاه دیگری نیستند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Before 2011, only small amounts of sargassum reached the Caribbean coast.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"the amounts were small enough to be ignored","why":{"en":"\"Very little of the seaweed reached the coasts... the amounts were small enough to be ignored.\"","tr":"\"Yosunun çok azı kıyılara ulaşıyordu... miktarlar görmezden gelinecek kadar küçüktü.\"","fa":"«مقدار خیلی کمی از جلبک به ساحل می‌رسید... آن‌قدر کم که نادیده گرفته می‌شد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most scientists believe that dust from the Sahara is the main cause of the blooms.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"there is no agreement about which matters most","why":{"en":"Sahara dust is one explanation; \"there is no agreement about which matters most\".","tr":"Sahra tozu açıklamalardan yalnızca biri; \"hangisinin en önemli olduğu konusunda uzlaşma yok\".","fa":"غبار صحرا فقط یکی از توضیح‌هاست؛ «توافقی نیست که کدام مهم‌تر است»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge","PARA-cause"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Hotels on affected islands have lowered their prices to attract visitors.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"holidaymakers stay away from beaches that smell bad","why":{"en":"The passage says holidaymakers stay away, but nothing about hotel prices.","tr":"Metin tatilcilerin uzak durduğunu söylüyor ama otel fiyatlarından söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید مسافرها دوری می‌کنند، اما درباره‌ی قیمت هتل‌ها چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Floating barriers cost less than collecting the seaweed with boats.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Floating barriers placed out at sea can guide it away from the shore","why":{"en":"Both methods are described, but their costs are not compared.","tr":"İki yöntem de anlatılıyor ama maliyetleri karşılaştırılmıyor.","fa":"هر دو روش توضیح داده شده‌اند، اما هزینه‌شان مقایسه نشده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 8-10. Complete the flow-chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"flow-chart","flowTitle":"Turning sargassum into fertiliser","flowEnd":"Dry the seaweed and mix it into compost","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Collect the seaweed before it begins to ___","accept":["rot"],"limit":2,"evidence":"collected before it starts to rot","why":{"en":"\"Collected before it starts to rot\": begins = starts.","tr":"\"Çürümeye başlamadan önce toplanır\": begins = starts.","fa":"«قبل از اینکه شروع به پوسیدن کند جمع می‌شود»: begins یعنی starts."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Wash it with fresh water to remove the ___","accept":["sea salt"],"limit":2,"evidence":"washed with fresh water to remove the sea salt","why":{"en":"\"Washed with fresh water to remove the sea salt, which would damage crops.\" Two words.","tr":"\"Ürünlere zarar verecek deniz tuzunu gidermek için tatlı suyla yıkanır.\" İki kelime.","fa":"«با آب شیرین شسته می‌شود تا نمک دریا که به محصول آسیب می‌زند پاک شود». دو کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Test it for ___ such as arsenic","accept":["heavy metals"],"limit":2,"evidence":"tested for heavy metals","why":{"en":"\"Tested for heavy metals, because sargassum can absorb substances such as arsenic.\" Plural, two words.","tr":"\"Ağır metaller için test edilir, çünkü sargassum arsenik gibi maddeleri emebilir.\" Çoğul, iki kelime.","fa":"«برای فلزات سنگین آزمایش می‌شود، چون سارگاسوم می‌تواند موادی مثل آرسنیک را جذب کند». جمع، دو کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-plural"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 11-13. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Other uses and plans","questions":[{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Other uses · Mexico: dried seaweed pressed into building ___","accept":["blocks"],"limit":1,"evidence":"pressed the dried seaweed into building blocks","why":{"en":"\"Pressed the dried seaweed into building blocks.\" \"building\" is printed; plural.","tr":"\"Kurutulmuş yosunu bastırarak yapı blokları yaptı.\" \"building\" yazılı; çoğul.","fa":"«جلبک خشک را به شکل بلوک ساختمانی پرس کرد». «building» چاپ شده؛ جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Other uses · also turned into ___","accept":["paper"],"limit":1,"evidence":"others have turned it into paper","why":{"en":"\"Others have turned it into paper.\"","tr":"\"Başkaları onu kâğıda dönüştürdü.\"","fa":"«دیگران آن را به کاغذ تبدیل کرده‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Other uses · satellite images give early ___ of mats heading for the coast","accept":["warnings"],"limit":1,"evidence":"give early warnings of large mats heading for the coast","why":{"en":"\"Systems that use satellite images to give early warnings.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Uydu görüntüleriyle erken uyarı veren sistemler.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«سیستم‌هایی که با تصویر ماهواره‌ای هشدار زودهنگام می‌دهند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]}]}],"id":"c-x04-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The nets were clogged with weed.\" Clogged means...","options":["torn","blocked","cleaned"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Clogged = blocked so that nothing can pass.","tr":"Clogged = hiçbir şey geçemeyecek şekilde tıkanmış.","fa":"clogged یعنی آن‌قدر گرفته که چیزی رد نمی‌شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"goes bad\". Which word would you look for in a passage?","options":["rots","floats","spreads"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"To rot = to decay and go bad.","tr":"Rot = çürümek, bozulmak.","fa":"rot یعنی پوسیدن و خراب شدن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Flow-chart: \"leaves dried and ___ into powder\" (NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS). The passage says \"the leaves are dried and crushed into a fine powder\". What do you write?","options":["crushed into","fine powder","crushed"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"into powder\" is printed, so one word fills the gap: crushed, in the same form as the passage.","tr":"\"into powder\" yazılı; boşluğu tek kelime doldurur: crushed, metindeki biçimle.","fa":"«into powder» چاپ شده، پس یک کلمه جای خالی را پر می‌کند: crushed، با همان شکل متن."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Some researchers blame warmer seas; others point to pollution.\" Statement: \"Researchers agree that warmer seas are to blame.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Two groups disagree, so \"researchers agree\" contradicts the text.","tr":"İki grup aynı fikirde değil; \"araştırmacılar hemfikir\" metinle çelişiyor.","fa":"دو گروه هم‌نظر نیستند، پس «پژوهشگران توافق دارند» با متن تناقض دارد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Tourists avoided the beach that summer.\" Statement: \"Hotels cut their prices that summer.\"","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The text is about tourists, not hotel prices.","tr":"Metin turistlerle ilgili, otel fiyatlarıyla değil.","fa":"متن درباره‌ی گردشگرهاست، نه قیمت هتل‌ها."}}],"id":"c-x04-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: adverts and listings","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: ilanlar ve tanıtımlar","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: آگهی‌ها و معرفی‌ها"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to check statements about a course advert as TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, watching for conditions, and to match facts to six short listings when a letter can be used more than once.","tr":"Bu derste bir kurs ilanıyla ilgili ifadeleri koşullara dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olarak kontrol etmeyi ve bir harfin birden fazla kullanılabildiği durumda bilgileri altı kısa tanıtımla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌هایی درباره‌ی آگهی یک دوره را با دقت به شرط‌ها به‌صورت TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN بررسی کنی و اطلاعات را به شش معرفی کوتاه وصل کنی، وقتی یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Listings","tr":"Tanıtım","fa":"معرفی"},"value":"A-F"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: climbing and gardens","tr":"Bu sınav: tırmanış ve bahçeler","fa":"این آزمون: کوه‌نوردی و باغ‌ها"},"intro":{"en":"Section 1 has short everyday texts. Adverts for courses, events and places to visit are the most frequent kind. They are full of conditions (if, unless, as long as) and small facts about prices, times and access.","tr":"Section 1 kısa günlük metinler içerir. Kurslar, etkinlikler ve gezilecek yerler için ilanlar en sık türdür. Koşullarla (if, unless, as long as) ve fiyatlar, saatler ve erişimle ilgili küçük bilgilerle doludur.","fa":"Section 1 متن‌های کوتاه روزمره دارد. آگهی دوره‌ها، برنامه‌ها و جاهای دیدنی پرتکرارترین نوع‌اند. پر از شرط‌اند (if، unless، as long as) و نکته‌های کوچک درباره‌ی قیمت، ساعت و دسترسی."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x04-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A course advert and six gardens","tr":"Bir kurs ilanı ve altı bahçe","fa":"آگهی یک دوره و شش باغ"},"asks":{"en":"Section 1 gives two short texts that advertise things: a beginners’ climbing course, and six gardens that are open to visitors. Adverts and listings are the most frequent GT Section 1 texts.","tr":"Section 1 bir şeylerin reklamını yapan iki kısa metin verir: yeni başlayanlar için bir tırmanış kursu ve ziyarete açık altı bahçe. İlanlar ve tanıtım listeleri GT Section 1’de en sık çıkan metinlerdir.","fa":"Section 1 دو متن کوتاه تبلیغاتی می‌دهد: یک دوره‌ی کوه‌نوردی برای مبتدی‌ها و شش باغ که برای بازدید باز هستند. آگهی‌ها و معرفی‌ها پرتکرارترین متن‌های GT Section 1 هستند."},"fields":["Who can join","When and where","Equipment","Price and booking","Opening times","Access","Children and dogs"],"words":[{"a":"no experience is needed","b":"complete beginners are welcome","tr":"deneyim gerekmez","fa":"تجربه لازم نیست"},{"a":"optional","b":"you can choose / not required","tr":"isteğe bağlı","fa":"اختیاری"},{"a":"weather permitting","b":"if the weather is good enough","tr":"hava izin verirse","fa":"اگر هوا اجازه بدهد"},{"a":"provided","b":"given to you","tr":"sağlanır","fa":"تأمین می‌شود"},{"a":"make up a session","b":"do it on another day","tr":"dersi telafi etmek","fa":"جلسه را جبران کردن"},{"a":"as long as","b":"only if","tr":"... şartıyla","fa":"به شرطی که"},{"a":"donations","b":"money you choose to give","tr":"bağışlar","fa":"کمک مالی"},{"a":"not suitable for wheelchairs","b":"wheelchairs cannot use it","tr":"tekerlekli sandalyeye uygun değil","fa":"مناسب ویلچر نیست"},{"a":"level paths","b":"flat paths","tr":"düz yollar","fa":"مسیرهای هموار"},{"a":"on leads","b":"tied, not running free","tr":"tasmalı","fa":"با قلاده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Conditions: \"parking is free, as long as you arrive before nine\" is not \"parking is always free\". A condition makes \"always\" FALSE.","tr":"Koşullar: \"dokuzdan önce gelirsen otopark ücretsiz\", \"otopark her zaman ücretsiz\" demek değildir. Bir koşul \"always\"i FALSE yapar.","fa":"شرط‌ها: «پارکینگ رایگان است، به شرطی که قبل از نه برسی» با «پارکینگ همیشه رایگان است» یکی نیست. یک شرط «always» را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Two listings can mention the same thing (\"dogs\"): one welcomes all dogs, another allows guide dogs only. Read the whole statement.","tr":"İki ilan aynı şeyden (\"dogs\") söz edebilir: biri bütün köpekleri kabul eder, diğeri yalnızca rehber köpeklere izin verir. İfadenin tamamını oku.","fa":"دو معرفی ممکن است از یک چیز («dogs») حرف بزنند: یکی همه‌ی سگ‌ها را می‌پذیرد و دیگری فقط سگ راهنما را. کل جمله را بخوان."}],"example":{"text":"\"Tickets can be bought on the door, unless the show is sold out in advance.\"","item":"Statement: You can always buy a ticket on the door. TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Unless the show is sold out\": not always.","tr":"\"Gösteri önceden tükenmediyse\": her zaman değil.","fa":"«مگر اینکه از قبل تمام شده باشد»: نه همیشه."}}},{"id":"GT1-ads","ctx":["GT1-ads"],"title":{"en":"Adverts and listings","tr":"İlanlar ve listeler","fa":"آگهی‌ها و فهرست‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"Short adverts or listings A-F for courses, events, campsites, tours or clubs. Questions ask which advert mentions a fact, or whether a statement is TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Kurslar, etkinlikler, kamp alanları, turlar ya da kulüpler için A-F harfli kısa ilanlar veya listeler. Sorular hangi ilanın bir bilgiden söz ettiğini ya da bir ifadenin TRUE, FALSE veya NOT GIVEN olduğunu sorar.","fa":"آگهی‌ها یا فهرست‌های کوتاه A تا F برای کلاس‌ها، رویدادها، کمپ‌ها، تورها یا باشگاه‌ها. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام آگهی به یک نکته اشاره می‌کند، یا یک جمله TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است."},"fields":["Which course is suitable for complete beginners?","Which event takes place outdoors?","Which campsite allows dogs?","Booking is required for all tours."],"words":[{"a":"suitable for beginners","b":"no experience needed","tr":"yeni başlayanlara uygun","fa":"مناسب مبتدی‌ها"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"at no cost / complimentary","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"booking essential","b":"places must be reserved","tr":"rezervasyon şart","fa":"رزرو الزامی"},{"a":"reduced price","b":"discount / 20% off","tr":"indirimli fiyat","fa":"قیمت با تخفیف"},{"a":"family-friendly","b":"children welcome","tr":"aileye uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"},{"a":"outdoors","b":"in the open air","tr":"açık havada","fa":"در فضای باز"},{"a":"pets allowed","b":"dogs welcome","tr":"evcil hayvan kabul edilir","fa":"ورود حیوان خانگی آزاد"},{"a":"on site","b":"at the campsite itself","tr":"tesis içinde","fa":"در خود محل"},{"a":"equipment provided","b":"everything supplied","tr":"ekipman sağlanır","fa":"تجهیزات داده می‌شود"},{"a":"refundable","b":"money back if you cancel","tr":"iade edilebilir","fa":"قابل استرداد"},{"a":"weekly","b":"once a week","tr":"haftalık","fa":"هفتگی"},{"a":"within walking distance","b":"nearby / a short walk away","tr":"yürüme mesafesinde","fa":"با پای پیاده نزدیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Matching: two adverts mention dogs, but only one allows them. Read the whole line.","tr":"Eşleştirme: iki ilan köpeklerden söz eder ama yalnızca biri izin verir. Satırın tamamını oku.","fa":"جورکردن: دو آگهی از سگ حرف می‌زنند، ولی فقط یکی اجازه می‌دهد. کل خط را بخوان."},{"en":"\"Free\" in one advert may mean free parking, not free entry.","tr":"Bir ilandaki \"free\" giriş değil, ücretsiz otopark anlamına gelebilir.","fa":"«free» در یک آگهی شاید یعنی پارکینگ رایگان، نه ورود رایگان."}],"example":{"text":"C  Lakeside Campsite. Quiet site by the water. Sorry, no dogs. Shop on site.\nD  Hilltop Farm Camping. Families and well-behaved pets welcome. Nearest shop 2 km.","item":"Which campsite allows dogs?","answer":"D","why":{"en":"Both mention dogs or pets. C says \"no dogs\"; D says \"pets welcome\".","tr":"İkisi de köpek ya da evcil hayvandan söz ediyor. C \"köpek yok\", D \"evcil hayvanlar kabul\" diyor.","fa":"هر دو از سگ یا حیوان خانگی حرف می‌زنند. C می‌گوید «سگ ممنوع»؛ D می‌گوید «حیوان خانگی پذیرفته می‌شود»."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Statements, then six listings","tr":"Önce ifadeler, sonra altı tanıtım","fa":"اول جمله‌ها، بعد شش معرفی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7 are TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN statements about the advert. Questions 8-14 ask which of six places, A-F, each statement is true for; a letter can be used more than once.","tr":"Soru 1-7 ilanla ilgili TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN ifadeleridir. Soru 8-14 her ifadenin altı yerden (A-F) hangisi için doğru olduğunu sorar; bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷ جمله‌های TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی آگهی‌اند. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴ می‌پرسند هر جمله درباره‌ی کدام یک از شش مکان (A تا F) درست است؛ یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Look for the condition","tr":"Koşulu ara","fa":"دنبال شرط بگرد"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline strong words in each statement: always, all, must, free.","tr":"Her ifadedeki güçlü kelimelerin altını çiz: always, all, must, free.","fa":"زیر کلمه‌های قوی هر جمله خط بکش: always، all، must، free."},{"en":"Find the sentence in the advert and look for a condition: if, unless, as long as, weather permitting.","tr":"İlandaki cümleyi bul ve bir koşul ara: if, unless, as long as, weather permitting.","fa":"جمله را در آگهی پیدا کن و دنبال شرط بگرد: if، unless، as long as، weather permitting."},{"en":"For the listings, check all six before you decide, because two may mention the same subject.","tr":"Tanıtımlarda karar vermeden önce altısına da bak, çünkü ikisi aynı konudan söz edebilir.","fa":"در معرفی‌ها قبل از تصمیم هر شش تا را نگاه کن، چون شاید دو تا از یک موضوع حرف بزنند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?","text":"\"Lockers are available for all students. A small deposit is returned when you hand back the key.\"","item":"Statement: Students must pay to use a locker.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: the sentence about lockers.","tr":"Yeri bul: dolaplarla ilgili cümle.","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: جمله‌ی مربوط به کمدها."},{"en":"A deposit is \"returned\": you get the money back.","tr":"Depozito \"iade ediliyor\": paranı geri alıyorsun.","fa":"ودیعه «پس داده می‌شود»: پولت را پس می‌گیری."},{"en":"Paying to use it goes against the text: FALSE.","tr":"Kullanmak için ödemek metinle çelişiyor: FALSE.","fa":"پول دادن برای استفاده با متن تناقض دارد: FALSE."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"The outdoor session goes ahead, weather permitting.\" Statement: \"The outdoor session will definitely take place.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Weather permitting\" means it may be cancelled, so \"definitely\" is wrong.","tr":"\"Hava izin verirse\" iptal edilebileceği anlamına gelir; \"kesinlikle\" yanlış.","fa":"«اگر هوا اجازه بدهد» یعنی شاید لغو شود، پس «حتماً» غلط است."}},"remember":{"en":"Strong words meet conditions: always against unless. Check all six listings before choosing.","tr":"Güçlü kelimeler koşullarla karşılaşır: always ile unless. Seçmeden önce altı tanıtımın hepsine bak.","fa":"کلمه‌های قوی با شرط‌ها روبه‌رو می‌شوند: always در برابر unless. قبل از انتخاب هر شش معرفی را نگاه کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x04-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"Climbing and gardens","tr":"Tırmanış ve bahçeler","fa":"کوه‌نوردی و باغ‌ها"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-ads"],"texts":[{"title":"Learn to climb at Granite Edge Climbing Centre","kind":"course advert","body":"Have you always wanted to try climbing? Our six-week Introduction to Climbing course is the perfect place to start. No experience is needed, and you don't need to be especially fit: our instructors will build up your strength and confidence step by step.\n\nThe course\nSessions take place on Tuesday evenings from 7 to 9 pm on our indoor climbing walls. In the first three weeks you will learn how to use a harness, how to tie the essential knots and how to hold the rope safely for a partner. In the second half of the course, you will climb more challenging routes and learn how to fall safely. On the final week, there is an optional trip to an outdoor crag, weather permitting; transport is not included.\n\nWho can join\nThe course is open to anyone aged 16 or over. Climbers aged 16 and 17 need a signed form from a parent. Groups are limited to eight people, so every climber gets plenty of attention.\n\nWhat to wear and bring\nWear loose, comfortable clothes that you can stretch in. Climbing shoes and a harness are provided free of charge for the whole course, so there's no need to buy your own equipment until you're sure you want to continue. Please bring a bottle of water; the café sells snacks.\n\nPrice and booking\nThe full course costs £95, which includes a free month of membership once you have finished. Places must be booked and paid for online. If you have to miss a session, you can make it up on the Thursday course at no extra cost, as long as there is space.\n\nAfter the course\nMany of our climbers go on to join our Monday club, where you can meet other climbers and improve at your own pace."},{"title":"Six gardens to visit this summer","kind":"six listings","body":"A  Holmwood House\nThe walled garden at this country house is famous for its roses, which are at their best in June. Guided tours with one of the gardeners run every Wednesday afternoon. There is a tea room in the old stables, and the house itself can be visited on a separate ticket.\n\nB  The Physic Garden\nCreated in the 1700s to grow plants used in medicine, this small city garden still has more than five hundred kinds of herbs. Labels explain what each plant was once used to treat. Entry is free, but donations are welcome. Because the garden is small, groups of more than ten must book in advance.\n\nC  Larchmere Arboretum\nThis collection of trees from around the world covers forty hectares, so allow at least half a day and wear strong shoes. Dogs on leads are welcome. Children can borrow a free activity pack from the visitor centre. The autumn colours in October attract huge crowds, so come early at weekends.\n\nD  Seacombe Gardens\nSheltered by the cliffs, this seaside garden grows palms and other plants that are rarely seen outdoors in this country. The steep paths are not suitable for wheelchairs. Open from April to October only. The small car park fills quickly, but a bus from the town centre stops at the gate every hour.\n\nE  The Willow Farm Maze\nThe garden here is planted around a huge maze made of living willow, which children love. There is also a large play area. Picnics are allowed anywhere in the grounds, and there is a covered area in case of rain.\n\nF  Kingfisher Water Garden\nBuilt around a series of ponds and streams, this garden is at its most colourful in late summer, when the water lilies flower. All paths are level and suitable for wheelchairs, and there are benches every fifty metres."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most people who take the course have climbed before.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"is the perfect place to start","why":{"en":"The advert says no experience is needed, but nothing about how many people have climbed before.","tr":"İlan deneyim gerekmediğini söylüyor ama kaç kişinin daha önce tırmandığından söz etmiyor.","fa":"آگهی می‌گوید تجربه لازم نیست، اما درباره‌ی اینکه چند نفر قبلاً کوه‌نوردی کرده‌اند چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Transport to the outdoor crag is provided by the centre.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"transport is not included","why":{"en":"The outdoor trip is optional, and \"transport is not included\".","tr":"Açık hava gezisi isteğe bağlı ve \"ulaşım dahil değil\".","fa":"سفر بیرونی اختیاری است و «حمل‌ونقل شامل نمی‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Climbers under 18 can join if a parent signs a form.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Climbers aged 16 and 17 need a signed form from a parent","why":{"en":"Open to 16 and over; \"climbers aged 16 and 17 need a signed form from a parent\".","tr":"16 yaş ve üstüne açık; \"16 ve 17 yaşındakiler bir ebeveynin imzaladığı formu getirmeli\".","fa":"برای ۱۶ سال به بالا باز است؛ «کوه‌نوردهای ۱۶ و ۱۷ ساله فرمی با امضای والدین لازم دارند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"There are no more than eight people in each group.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Groups are limited to eight people","why":{"en":"\"Limited to eight\" = no more than eight.","tr":"\"Sekiz kişiyle sınırlı\" = en fazla sekiz.","fa":"«محدود به هشت نفر» یعنی حداکثر هشت."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Climbing shoes are lent to climbers at no cost during the course.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Climbing shoes and a harness are provided free of charge for the whole course","why":{"en":"\"Provided free of charge for the whole course\" = lent at no cost.","tr":"\"Kurs boyunca ücretsiz sağlanır\" = ücretsiz ödünç verilir.","fa":"«در تمام دوره رایگان در اختیار گذاشته می‌شود» یعنی بی‌هزینه قرض داده می‌شود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"All the instructors are qualified mountain guides.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"our instructors will build up your strength and confidence step by step","why":{"en":"The instructors are mentioned, but not their qualifications.","tr":"Eğitmenlerden söz ediliyor ama nitelikleri belirtilmiyor.","fa":"از مربی‌ها اسم برده شده، اما نه از مدرک‌هایشان."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Climbers can always make up a missed session on Thursdays.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"as long as there is space","why":{"en":"Only \"as long as there is space\", so not always.","tr":"Yalnızca \"yer olduğu sürece\"; yani her zaman değil.","fa":"فقط «به شرطی که جا باشد»، پس نه همیشه."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Look at the six gardens, A-F, in the text. Which garden is each of the following statements true for? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A Holmwood House","B The Physic Garden","C Larchmere Arboretum","D Seacombe Gardens","E The Willow Farm Maze","F Kingfisher Water Garden"],"questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"match","prompt":"a place where you can learn how plants were once used to treat illness","correct":1,"evidence":"Labels explain what each plant was once used to treat","why":{"en":"B: a garden created to grow medicinal plants; labels explain what each one treated.","tr":"B: tıbbi bitkiler yetiştirmek için kurulmuş bir bahçe; etiketler her birinin neyi tedavi ettiğini anlatıyor.","fa":"B: باغی برای پرورش گیاهان دارویی؛ برچسب‌ها می‌گویند هر کدام چه چیزی را درمان می‌کرد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"match","prompt":"a garden that is closed for part of the year","correct":3,"evidence":"Open from April to October only","why":{"en":"D: \"Open from April to October only.\"","tr":"D: \"Yalnızca nisandan ekime kadar açık.\"","fa":"D: «فقط از آوریل تا اکتبر باز است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"match","prompt":"a garden that wheelchair users can easily get around","correct":5,"evidence":"All paths are level and suitable for wheelchairs","why":{"en":"F: \"All paths are level and suitable for wheelchairs.\" D’s paths are \"not suitable\".","tr":"F: \"Bütün yollar düz ve tekerlekli sandalyeye uygun.\" D’nin yolları \"uygun değil\".","fa":"F: «همه‌ی مسیرها هموار و مناسب ویلچرند». مسیرهای D «مناسب نیستند»."},"trap":["TR-samewords","TR-detail"]},{"n":11,"kind":"match","prompt":"guided tours on a particular day of the week","correct":0,"evidence":"Guided tours with one of the gardeners run every Wednesday afternoon","why":{"en":"A: \"Guided tours... every Wednesday afternoon.\"","tr":"A: \"Rehberli turlar... her çarşamba öğleden sonra.\"","fa":"A: «تورهای راهنمادار... هر چهارشنبه بعدازظهر»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"match","prompt":"a place where visitors may bring their dogs","correct":2,"evidence":"Dogs on leads are welcome","why":{"en":"C: \"Dogs on leads are welcome.\"","tr":"C: \"Tasmalı köpekler kabul ediliyor.\"","fa":"C: «سگ‌ها با قلاده پذیرفته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"match","prompt":"a garden that you do not have to pay to enter","correct":1,"evidence":"Entry is free, but donations are welcome","why":{"en":"B again: \"Entry is free\", although donations are welcome. B is used twice.","tr":"Yine B: \"Giriş ücretsiz\", bağış kabul edilse de. B iki kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"باز هم B: «ورود رایگان است»، هرچند کمک مالی پذیرفته می‌شود. B دو بار می‌آید."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-detail"]},{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"a place that children particularly enjoy","correct":4,"evidence":"which children love","why":{"en":"E: the willow maze, \"which children love\", and a large play area. C only lends activity packs.","tr":"E: çocukların \"çok sevdiği\" söğüt labirenti ve büyük bir oyun alanı. C yalnızca etkinlik paketi veriyor.","fa":"E: هزارتوی بید که «بچه‌ها عاشقش‌اند» و یک زمین بازی بزرگ. C فقط بسته‌ی سرگرمی قرض می‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]}],"id":"c-x04-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The trip is optional.\" This means you...","options":["must go","have to pay extra","can choose whether to go"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Optional = you decide; it is not required.","tr":"Optional = sen karar verirsin; zorunlu değil.","fa":"optional یعنی خودت تصمیم می‌گیری؛ اجباری نیست."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"only if the weather is good\"?","options":["whatever the weather","weather permitting","in all weathers"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Weather permitting\" = if the weather allows it.","tr":"\"Weather permitting\" = hava izin verirse.","fa":"«weather permitting» یعنی اگر هوا اجازه بدهد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Two listings both mention wheelchairs. How do you decide which matches \"easy for wheelchair users\"?","options":["Read both: one may say the paths are not suitable","Choose the first one you find","Choose the longer listing"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The same word can appear in a negative statement; check the whole sentence.","tr":"Aynı kelime olumsuz bir cümlede geçebilir; bütün cümleyi kontrol et.","fa":"یک کلمه ممکن است در جمله‌ای منفی بیاید؛ کل جمله را چک کن."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"You can change your booking free of charge, as long as you tell us 48 hours before.\" Statement: \"Bookings can always be changed for free.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The condition \"as long as you tell us 48 hours before\" makes \"always\" wrong.","tr":"\"48 saat önceden haber verdiğin sürece\" koşulu \"always\"i yanlış yapar.","fa":"شرطِ «به شرطی که ۴۸ ساعت قبل خبر بدهی» «always» را غلط می‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x04-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-04","unit":"x04-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
